# Steamworks: Steamworks SDK start, callbacks and shutdown

Check the result of SteamAPI_Init/InitEx and handle a failed start; call SteamAPI_RestartAppIfNecessary before it so the game relaunches through Steam; run callbacks every frame (SteamAPI_RunCallbacks) unless the wrapper does it for you; call SteamAPI_Shutdown on exit.

## The result of the Steam API start is not checked (error)

- Why: SteamAPI_Init fails when Steam is not running or the app id is wrong; the game then crashes or loses achievements silently at the first Steam call.
- Fix: Check the result (if (!SteamAPI_Init()) ...) and show a message or quit when Steam could not start.
- Source: https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/sdk/api#initialization_and_shutdown

## Steam callbacks are never run (error)

- Why: Without SteamAPI_RunCallbacks no Steam event arrives (overlay, lobbies, stats received, purchases).
- Fix: Call SteamAPI_RunCallbacks (SteamAPI.RunCallbacks in Steamworks.NET, Steam.run_callbacks in GodotSteam) once per frame.
- Source: https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/sdk/api#callbacks

## SteamAPI_RestartAppIfNecessary is not called (warning)

- Why: Without it, a player who starts the executable directly gets a game without Steam (no overlay, no achievements) instead of a relaunch through Steam.
- Fix: Call SteamAPI_RestartAppIfNecessary(<app id>) first and quit when it returns true.
- Source: https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/sdk/api#SteamAPI_RestartAppIfNecessary

## SteamAPI_Shutdown is not called (info)

- Why: Shutting the API down on exit lets Steam know the game stopped and releases its resources.
- Fix: Call SteamAPI_Shutdown (SteamAPI.Shutdown, SteamClient.Shutdown) when the game quits.
- Source: https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/sdk/api#initialization_and_shutdown

With the steamworks-mcp server connected, `check_code(path)` finds these problems in the whole project, with file and line (`check_code(path, rules=["steamworks-sdk-lifecycle"])` for this group only).
